# Copy to /etc/caddy/Caddyfile (or run: caddy run --config ./Caddyfile)
# Replace the domain with yours. Point DNS A/AAAA records to this server.
# Install Caddy: https://caddyserver.com/docs/install
#
# --- Option A: Full stack in Docker (nginx UI on host port 8080) ----------
# Testers open ONE URL: https://app.example.com (UI + API + WebSocket same origin)

# app.example.com {
#     reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080
# }

# --- Option B: API only on host (Vercel serves the UI) -------------------
# Set VITE_BACKEND_URL=https://api.example.com on Vercel.
# In server .env: ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://your-app.vercel.app

# api.example.com {
#     reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8000
# }

# Firewall: allow 80/443 (and SSH). Do NOT expose 9200, 9300, or 5601 publicly.
